<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine carmaker Sevel '96 net $21.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentine carmaker Sevel '96 net $21.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net $21.4 million vs n/a.</p>
<p>NOTE: Sevel, Argentine licensee of France's Peugeot, told the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange Monday that 1996 included an extraordinary loss of $17.8 million.</p>
<p>Sevel did not provide comparative figures, but in 1995 it reported a $127 million net loss that included an extraordinary loss of $83 million.</p>
<p>It did not report per share, revenue or quarterly figures.</p>
<p>The company said that in December 1996 its net worth stood at $387 million.</p>
<p>((-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
